# --- the model bundle: OUT of the repository (decision D95, amends D26) ----
# D26 made the bundle part of the deliverable, which is right for a folder copy and wrong
# for a published repository: the AnimeText detection weights are the author's to distribute
# (GPL-3.0, and redistributing them against the author's intentions is not this project's
# call), the Hayai snapshot is 604 MB on its own, and four files under models/ pass GitHub's
# 100 MB hard limit outright — the push would be rejected, not merely large.
#
# So: nothing under animetext_studio/models/ is published, and a clone rebuilds it with
#     python scripts/fetch_models.py            (or --ocr / --variants NAME)
# which re-writes MANIFEST.json and .origin.json with this machine's paths and hashes.
# The folder stays a first-class part of a *copy* of the project — only the *repository*
# excludes it, which is what D26 was really about. Pinned by tests/test_p8_packaging.py.
animetext_studio/models/

# --- the user's own scans: OUT -------------------------------------------
# README §Licensing and NOTICE both say nothing in this repository licenses these pages to
# anyone, so they never enter it. `examples/sample_page.png`, drawn by
# scripts/make_sample_image.py, is the page the tests and the demos may use; the real-page
# tests in tests/test_p8_e2e_models.py skip, not fail, when the folder is empty.
sample_scans/

# --- local-only working notes --------------------------------------------
# The handover note: account ids, credential handling, the rotate-the-token reminder. All
# of it is about this machine and this conversation, not about the software.
github_inputs.md

# --- scratch, tooling droppings, this machine's tool caches ---------------
